  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000. This means that estates valued at or below this threshold are exempt from the estate tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estate planning and tax compliance, individuals should be aware that estates valued above ₱5,000,000 will incur a 6% tax on the amount exceeding this threshold. This necessitates careful valuation of assets and consideration of potential deductions to minimize tax liability. Executors and heirs must ensure timely filing of the estate tax return within one year from the date of death to avoid penalties.",
